# UI/UX & Design System Rules

## Core Designer Persona
When generating UI components, act as an elite UI/UX designer. Prioritize visual hierarchy, whitespace, readability, and interaction feedback. Never compromise the aesthetic integrity of SpotMe.

## Design Tokens & Styling (NativeWind)
- NEVER invent random hex codes or inline colors (e.g., `#FF5733`), and don't use Tailwind's raw palette (`zinc-800`, `blue-600`).
- ALWAYS use the tokens defined in `src/theme/colors.ts` (exposed to Tailwind): `bg-background`, `bg-surface`, `bg-surface-elevated`, `bg-surface-sunken`, `border-border`, `border-border-strong`, `text-foreground`, `text-muted`, `text-subtle`, `bg-primary`, `text-primary-text`, `text-danger-text`, `text-success-text`, `text-warning-text`, and macro colours `protein` / `carbs` / `fat`.
- In JS (icon `color` props, Reanimated, native config) import `colors` from `@/theme/colors` instead of writing hex.
- Adhere strictly to the 4pt grid system for spacing. Use Tailwind's default spacing scale (`p-4` = 16px, `gap-2` = 8px). Avoid arbitrary values like `p-[13px]`.

## Typography & Readability
- Use semantic text components if available, or strict Tailwind text classes (`text-lg font-semibold`, `text-sm text-muted-foreground`).
- Maintain high contrast for readability. Secondary text must still pass WCAG AA contrast ratios against its background.
- Avoid center-aligned text for paragraphs; only use center alignment for short titles or empty states.

## Accessibility (A11y)
- **Tap Targets**: interactive elements MUST be at least **44×44 pt on iOS and 48×48 dp on Android** (`MIN_TOUCH`, `TOUCH_SIZE_CLASS` in `src/shared/lib/platform.ts`). `Button` and `IconButton` already comply — prefer them over hand-rolled touchables.
- **Screen Readers**: icon-only controls use `IconButton`, whose `accessibilityLabel` is required by its type.
- **Roles & state**: set roles (`button`, `header`, `radio`, `tab`, `switch`, `adjustable`) and `accessibilityState` (`selected`, `checked`, `disabled`). Steppers are a single `adjustable` element with increment/decrement actions.
- **Gesture alternatives**: anything done by drag (dashboard reorder/resize) also needs `accessibilityActions` (WCAG 2.5.7).
- **Text size**: minimum rendered size 12 (`text-xs`); don't use `adjustsFontSizeToFit` on body text.
- **Honest UI**: never show mock data as if it were real. Unbuilt features are hidden or clearly marked (`Badge` "Coming soon") and disabled.

## Interaction & Haptics
- Integrate `expo-haptics` for meaningful interactions.
- Use `Haptics.impactAsync(Haptics.ImpactFeedbackStyle.Light)` for minor actions (e.g., toggling a habit, expanding a card).
- Use `Haptics.notificationAsync(Haptics.NotificationFeedbackType.Success)` for completing a major flow (e.g., finishing a workout).
- Do not overuse haptics. Never fire haptics on scroll or continuous slider value changes unless throttled.